COVERAGE: 7 of 9 consumers have a demand model; wpResolver is UNKNOWN (charged 0
in 1 days) and ambientFetchLiveOdds is printed IF SERVED, apart. 224 game rows read, 33 with
no usable start_time: the CFL day count and the World Cup upper bound read them; every
other model skips them. Demand is a FLOOR of need under each model stated in the header
— a cadence above it is a product choice, not measured need. CI-triggered calls (probes,
the deploy step) are traffic and sit inside "charged", not "demand". The vendor may not
list every scheduled game (preseason, unlisted leagues); such games still count as demand.
